    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u quickly summarize the actual steps a company has to follow when someone submits a \"right to be forgotten\" request under gdpr? just need the main points for a memo.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a summary of the main steps a company must follow when processing a \"right to be forgotten\" request under GDPR:\n\n1. Receive and register the request: The request must be in writing and signed by the individual, and it should be registered in a logbook to track the request.\n2. Verify the request: The company must verify the individual's identity and confirm that they are the subject of the personal data in question.\n3. Acknowledge the request: The company must acknowledge the request and respond to the individual within 1-2 weeks, stating that it will be processed.\n4. Determine the scope: The company must determine what personal data is concerned and will be deleted or rectified.\n5. Consult data protection officials (if necessary): The company may need to consult with data protection officials or seek guidance from the relevant data protection authority.\n6. Process the request: The company must then process the request, either by deleting or rectifying the personal data.\n7. Communicate the outcome: The company must communicate the result of the processing, including any issues that prevented deletion, to the individual.\n\nNote: Compliance with GDPR requirements may vary depending on the specific circumstances and Regulatory requirements.",
