      "content": "In such cases, the GDPR controller must take reasonable steps to deidentify, anonymize, or permanently delete the personal data, even if it's no longer in active use. If the data is stored on old hardware or systems that are no longer accessible, the controller may:\n\n1. Ensure access only for purposes of data minimization (only access for deleted data)\n2. Create a newer system or centralized repository to hold the deleted data\n3. Ensure that the old system or hardware is permanently deleted or wiped of any personal data)\n\nThe key is to demonstrate that the controller has taken \"reasonable\" and \"technical\" measures to minimize the risk of re-identification. A written justification or audit trail can help demonstrate the effort taken to address the risk of retained data.",
